## 12. Start, Stop, and Restart Containers

Assume the container name is `web`.

### Stop a running container

```bash
docker stop web
```

Stops the container gracefully.

### Start a stopped container

```bash
docker start web
```

Starts the existing container again.

### Restart a container

```bash
docker restart web
```

Stops and starts the existing container.

### Important distinction

Stopping a container does not remove it.

```text
docker stop  = Stop the container
docker start = Start the existing container
docker rm    = Remove the container
```

